Date: Mon, 10 May 1993 15:03:36 -0600
From: twb3@midway.uchicago.edu (Tom Morrow)
Subject: Meta: Privatizing Judges

I'm very encouraged by this thread.  It seems to me as if we are reaching a
consensus on a method that will allow both allow us more freedom to choose
legal methods on this list and improve the peace of our virtual community.

As I currently understand that consensus, everyone who has posted on the
topic agrees that list members should have the right to choose third
parties to adjudicate their disputes.  They need not notify the List
Administrator of their privately-adjudicated disputes, but the LA retains
the right to bring separate charges for violation of the list's rules.

There is at least one topic that I think we still need to discuss, however.
 Robin has said that:

>I think the question is whether ExI will honor contracts made before a
>dispute has arisen, about who should judge any disputes between two
>parties.  . . . If they agreed to used judge A,
>and then one side changes their mind once a dispute has arisen, the
>List Administrator refuses to judge the case.

This sounds as if Robin wants the default rule to be: The LA will not hear
a case involving a party who refuses to honor a prior agreement to use a
private adjudicator.  But I am not sure that this is the optimal rule for
ensuring that the disputes get settled.  I would prefer to say that the LA
will honor adjudication contracts that explicitly say the LA is not to be
used.  Of course, as always, the LA retains the right to bring separate
charges.  But the default rule would be that anyone can make recourse to
the LA's services.  Parties must contract around this default rule.

I think this is consistent with Robin's restatement of his proposal:

>I hereby officially propose that ExI honor private prior contracts
>specifying who should judge future disputes regarding Extropy rules.


I will try to encourage, or at least leave room for, the PPL reforms we
have been suggesting as I revise the List Code.

T.O. Morrow                     --  twb3@midway.uchicago.edu
Vice President: ExI             --  The Extropy Institute
Law & Politics Editor: EXTROPY  --  Journal of Transhumanist Thought


